WEBVTT

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.720
Natsu!

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.060
Are you okay, Natsu?

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.310
How stupid can you get?

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.730
I just knew we would find trouble
going into a dangerous place on purpose.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.070
This is just like
what we experienced before.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.620
<i>Or could we still be lost underground
in the depths of that cave?</i>

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.500
<i>Until we climb up this rocky cliff again,
this test will not come to an end.</i>

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.170
<i>I'll climb up again with Shigeru.</i>

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.670
<i>This time, I will save Shigeru.</i>

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.550
<i>Shigeru... Natsu...</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.730
Ouch!

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.730
The ship tipped sideways.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.650
Then it's about to be flooded!

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.570
I need to run. I need to get outside.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.450
Where is Ango?

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.870
Ango?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:19.820
Ango!

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.540
Semimaru? Ms. Botan? Where are you?

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.040
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.790
<i>Orientation transition is complete.</i>

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.880
<i>Doors on all passageways
have been unlocked.</i>

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.050
Excuse me. Can you hear me?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.220
Is anybody out there?

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.230
<i>I repeat,
orientation transition is complete.</i>

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.900
<i>Doors on all passageways
have been unlocked.</i>

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.070
I'm alone?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.160
WINTER BEGINS

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.410
The ship stopped.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.420
What is that?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.550
The doors that were on the ground

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.010
are now in their proper position
after turning 90 degrees.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.260
Does that mean they made them
knowing the ship would turn vertical?

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.010
Good guess. It seems so.

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.100
The stairs match the current orientation
and head downward.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.020
Really?

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.940
But wait. What about everybody
who went inside?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.690
They must be in trouble
since everything turned sideways, right?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.320
It's their fault for going in.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.700
We have to go save them.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.950
That's risky.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.870
Right...

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.290
But I'm worried.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.870
If you don't like getting on ships,
you can wait here, Ryo.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.170
I'm going to go look for them.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.920
I have to get Ango out of there too.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.130
Ryo?

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.130
Proceed with caution.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.260
Don't assume things are secure.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.890
Watch your footing
and have a way out when descending.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:28.890
Got that?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.140
Yes. Thanks a lot, Ryo!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.400
What the hell was that?
Did the ship just sink?

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.350
It seems like it.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.110
The door we used is now on the ceiling.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.860
The ship capsized?

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.780
-Are you okay, Hotaru?
-What are we going to do?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.150
-Yes. Please have a look at this.
-This is bad!

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.950
-It seems to be a map of this ship.
-We shouldn't have come here!

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.740
-It says "Fuji."
-We never should have come!

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.160
-So the name of this ship is H.M.S. Fuji.
-Oh, god! Run away!

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.080
-How can anybody remain calm?
-This must be the eighth Fuji location.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.710
Wait, isn't that picture of the ship
vertical?

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.960
Yes. That's how it is now.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.880
-It seems this is the proper orientation.
-What?

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.130
That's right, Ms. Botan.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.840
I've seen similar things on TV before.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.350
Ships used for ocean research
and the like can turn vertically.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.060
They can float vertically, just like
the fishing bobbers fisherman use.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.270
The waves have less effect on it.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.320
And even if it's hit by strong winds,
it won't capsize.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:25.320
That's probably how this ship survived
the disaster that ended the world.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.990
This ship must be a shelter.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.370
<i>They built the eighth storage shelter
on the sea.</i>

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.670
There are many doors.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.670
Is it okay to open them?
Is it okay for me to move?

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.840
<i>When I was little, I was too scared
to ride the elevator by myself.</i>

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.930
<i>I was afraid that I would get trapped
if something went wrong.</i>

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.560
<i>I can't do anything by myself.
I just know I'll screw up.</i>

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.060
<i>Should I just wait here patiently?</i>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.190
<i>But what if it floods with water?</i>

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.570
<i>Just stay calm, Natsu.</i>

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.160
<i>It's not pitch black for the time being.</i>

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:15.750
<i>I can't go back up to where I fell from,
so isn't trying the doors my only option?</i>

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.300
Is this somebody's room?

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.190
Please save me...

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.490
A kitty?

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.200
Why?

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.200
MIMI

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:54.990
Is its name "Mimi"?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.870
I found it.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.880
Hey! Everybody! I'm back!

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.550
Hey!

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.340
Arashi!

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.930
Arashi!

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.350
Chimaki? What are you doing?

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.390
I fell and got tangled,
so I couldn't get out.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.310
But at the same time,
I didn't end up drowning thanks to that.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:26.980
Thanks.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.490
The water was very cold.
I thought I would be in trouble soon.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.410
Hey, Chimaki. Your clothes are dyed green.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.580
Really? I wonder if I can get
green pigment from them.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.830
How can you be so unconcerned?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.580
This area is packed with algae, isn't it?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.330
Indeed. It's all around the ship too.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.300
But the area directly under the ship
was not as densely packed with algae.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.590
Why do you think that is?

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.260
I don't know.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:56.010
So what about everyone else?

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.470
Why didn't they come to save you?

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.480
Because they all left to go to that ship.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:02.980
They're inside?

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.770
You're going?

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.650
They might need my help.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.860
You should rest
and get warmed up, Chimaki.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.870
<i>Nobody will come to save me.</i>

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.080
<i>I need to take action on my own.</i>

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.130
It sounds hollow.

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.170
That means there isn't water
on the other side.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.680
Let's go together, Mimi.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:42.770
Let's look for an exit
and for everyone else.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.940
NATSU

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.110
What the hell is this?

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.320
Bodies, it would seem.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.740
Semimaru. Don't touch anything.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.740
That wall was the floor
until a few minutes ago.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:01.660
Guns?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.700
There are more over here.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.830
Wow, you're right.
There are pistols and rifles.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.540
Are they real? No way.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:14.260
Awesome! Model guns everywhere!

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.970
They're all rusty, though.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.890
The room next door has more of the same.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.050
I see.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.680
Across the hall too.
They're full of weapons.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.310
So that's how it is.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.600
They were hiding them from us.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:29.650
Although this ship is a warehouse,
it's also an arsenal.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.860
An arsenal? So these are all real?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.570
What in the world is this?

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:38.200
It's a warehouse, right?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.620
I feel like I'm only getting
farther from an exit.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.000
What's that?

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.160
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.460
"Final Day"?

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.960
And the time is running out?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.130
<i>There are 13 minutes left.</i>

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.920
<i>But what does "time remaining" mean?</i>

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.880
<i>Is it the time left until the ship sinks?</i>

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.760
<i>Is this ship just slowly sinking
after it turned vertically?</i>

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.140
There is no way for me to go up.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.310
Mimi!

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.610
"Vertical shift"?

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:18.110
"Hull currently stable"?

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.620
What are these about?
Are all these readings accurate?

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:23.990
So the ship isn't sinking?

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:26.000
It turned vertically on purpose?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.620
But why? Is this ship built for that?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:38.630
<i>I was trying to calm myself down,
but I ended up panicking for a second.</i>

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.220
Now that I look closely,
I see it says 13 hours, not 13 minutes.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:45.510
I can't see things...

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:50.560
You can't see what's happening,
so that’s why you screw up, Natsu.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.110
YOUR LOCATION
C BLOCK, M WAREHOUSE NORTH SIDE

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.070
So I'm this far down, in C Block...

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:59.030
There's a way up!

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.450
<i>If you closely observe your surroundings,
you'll see there's always a way.</i>

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:10.210
<i>Right. I have to pay close attention,
so I can explain it all to everyone later.</i>

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.710
<i>Even in that last room I was in,</i>

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.460
<i>if I had looked closer,
I could have found something useful.</i>

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.470
<i>But the skeletons scared me
and I couldn't see anything else.</i>

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.430
I'm sorry, Mimi.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:24.850
This time for sure, I'll stay calm.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:34.730
Wow! So these are real guns! How cool!

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:36.610
Semimaru. Don't touch them.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.650
If they're loaded,
that might accidentally go off.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:42.410
Guns that aren't cleaned properly
can malfunction.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:49.410
<i>Even so, perhaps I should consider
taking one for myself.</i>

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.210
<i>If Ango and Ryo both have one,
shouldn't I have one too?</i>

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:54.750
Ms. Botan.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.290
What is it, Hotaru?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.920
I took a quick look
in several of the rooms in this area,

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:03.380
<i>but the things inside them
had different orientations.</i>

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.600
<i>Some were horizontal,
others were still vertical,</i>

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.390
<i>and some furniture were even leaning over.</i>

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:15.190
Normally, the rooms would be designed
to match the ship when it goes vertical.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.520
But either there isn't enough power
or only some are functioning.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.530
That's what it seemed like.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:23.030
It seems really inconvenient.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.870
<i>Something must be wrong with me.</i>

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:27.990
<i>Did I plan on having a gunfight?</i>

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.790
Big Sis, I'm going to go search for Natsu.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.540
When she sees all this crazy stuff,
she'll get scared and not do anything.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:40.210
I mean, Ango is probably with her now,
which is kind of a relief.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.720
But, on the other hand,
it might be trouble as well!

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.390
Hotaru! Quit laughing! I'll smack you!

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:48.260
We're searching for her right now.

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:51.720
Right, but I was planning to look for her
back where we came from.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.730
Back where we came from?

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:57.860
Semimaru! We need to stick together!

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.320
This is dangerous for Hotaru.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.450
You and her should look for
a way out from that side.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:05.740
I'll see you later!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.570
Semimaru! Be careful!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.830
Mr. Semimaru will be okay.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.120
As if.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:15.040
More importantly, Ms. Botan,
there's a room over here that bothers me.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.460
I'm invincible. This is so cool!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:23.380
Just wait for me, Natsu.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:30.180
Ryo, are you checking
the hull strength with that?

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.890
That's part of it,
but it's mainly a signal.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:34.140
A signal?

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.560
If it reaches Ango, he will understand it.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.650
Yelling out loud is something
only idiots do.

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:41.150
Really?

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:42.820
Don't lean on the handrail.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.070
What?

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.700
Don't put all your weight in one place.
And watch out for floor discoloration.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.110
Right.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.450
We shouldn't have come here
in the first place.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.160
Entering dangerous places like this
only leads to suffering.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.620
Danger is meant to be avoided.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.090
Well, sure.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.590
That was true for the world
we used to live in.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.800
It was clear which places were dangerous
and which places were not, you know?

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.970
But now, it's not as clear.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.270
Or rather, you can't really be certain
of one or the other.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:18.560
We're not in a place
where staying put makes you any safer.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:23.230
In this world, the safe places
and the dangerous ones are the same.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.110
Even this ship,
while it might be dangerous,

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:30.410
if we find something good,
we'll be glad we came in the end.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.450
Don't you think that's true, Ryo?

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.290
Ryo?

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.500
You know, you're surprisingly clever.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.000
What? You think so? Hooray!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.670
<i>What was that?
Some thought just crossed my mind.</i>

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.250
<i>I felt like I understood something.</i>

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.170
<i>But it slipped away before I could.</i>

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:52.010
It bothers me that he said "surprisingly,"
but I won't let it bother me.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.470
<i>I doubt there's anything a dropout
like her could make me realize, right?</i>

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.520
<i>Ango, if you hear this, reply.</i>

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.480
<i>This enclosed space is not good for you.</i>

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.610
<i>Let's get out of here quickly.</i>

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.860
<i>Where are you, Ango?</i>

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.780
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.040
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:20.080
<i>It's a continuation of the test.</i>

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:22.210
<i>This is an underground cave.</i>

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.500
<i>Shigeru... we'll do it over.</i>

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.050
Shigeru! Where are you, Shigeru?

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.840
So, Ryo, why do you hate being on ships?

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:36.220
Because I was almost killed
inside an abandoned ship once.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:38.810
What? Killed? By who?

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:40.310
One of the professors.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.100
What the heck? A demented professor?

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:45.690
How terrible! That's awful!
Were they arrested?

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:49.280
The ship exploded, and then later,
he apparently committed suicide.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.780
What a lowlife!

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.450
That must have been hard on you, Ryo.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:56.080
But that guy was just a weakling.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.240
You're way stronger than him now, Ryo.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.660
He can't do anything to you anymore!

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:03.420
He's not even in this world!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:06.210
There's nothing to be afraid of!
It's okay now, Ryo.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.380
Right.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.130
<i>Something seems off.</i>

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.470
<i>But, well...</i>

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:14.760
This ship is off too.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.930
What's with that? We're stuck now!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.350
Wow, Ryo! Amazing! Be careful.

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:27.560
Get the rope over there.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.360
And then what should I do?

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:30.360
Jump.

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:38.280
This ship is simply unbelievable.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.870
So, this position is possible.
It is floating like normal.

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.920
When it was horizontal, it used the wind,

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.750
and when it was vertical,
it used waves to produce electricity.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.340
And it used solar power.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.170
It might even be connected to
those windmills by cables.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.010
That means it must have needed
a lot of power.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:00.390
The lights are on!

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:02.810
Amazing.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.730
How many days has it been?

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:08.110
I had already gotten pretty used to life
without any electricity.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:13.610
Hey! Guys! Is there anybody in here?

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:20.780
There are no stairs.

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.790
Even though there's a door,
how am I supposed to get there?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:25.620
What do I do?

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.460
<i>Look closely.</i>

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.460
<i>Look closely.</i>

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.550
<i>Figure it out yourself.</i>

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.350
What?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.150
Natsu, I'm here to save you!

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:51.940
I'm on the SWAT team.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.360
It's okay, Natsu. I'll keep you safe.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:56.990
Just kidding.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.610
Damn, I'm cool.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.330
I wish we could bring back
a few guns we can use.

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:04.330
They would be useful for hunting animals.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.210
And we can use them to repel Team Autumn
if we cross paths again.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.710
Weird. When did I cut myself?

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.710
Ever since coming here,

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:18.550
I've been getting lots of cuts
and bruises without realizing it.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.600
Is somebody there?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:27.480
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.520
<i>Just now, I felt something. What is it?</i>

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:33.020
<i>I've got goosebumps.</i>

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.320
<i>Is something watching me?</i>

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.240
<i>I'm really sensitive to stuff like that,</i>

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:43.700
<i>since I was bullied a lot as a kid.</i>

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.580
This room over here.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:47.500
CAPTAIN'S QUARTERS

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:48.540
The captain's quarters.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.580
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:55.050
"Final Day"? For what?

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:58.550
The time remaining is counting down.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:02.510
There's one video file here.
Shall we play it?

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:03.510
NEW FILE 1

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.230
<i>Greetings to all aboard.</i>

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.270
<i>This is your captain speaking.</i>

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.940
Hey! Guys! Anybody there?

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:17.990
A water tank?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:26.950
<i>We survived that horrible disaster
along with the H.M.S. Fuji.</i>

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:32.960
<i>We believed that a new world would come,
and that this was to be its Noah's Ark.</i>

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:35.710
<i>But the Earth has continued to cool,</i>

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.210
<i>and we haven't been able to
release a single dove.</i>

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.420
<i>There is no sign that it will recover.</i>

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:46.560
<i>The fuel has been exhausted
and the food supplies have run out.</i>

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:50.180
<i>There is hardly any power left
to keep the ship heated.</i>

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:55.020
<i>How much longer will we continue
to survive like this?</i>

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:58.940
<i>The god of reason was enshrined
on the bow of this ship.</i>

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:04.950
<i>However, it seems that we have begun
to lose our sense of reason.</i>

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.870
<i>We are completely isolated.</i>

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.790
<i>Replies to our messages have ceased,</i>

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:15.290
<i>and those aboard have now
begun to kill each other.</i>

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:20.630
<i>There is nothing left that can hold back
the madness and despair.</i>

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.800
<i>Therefore, I have made up my mind.</i>

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:29.970
<i>Everyone, let us bring all of this
to an end.</i>

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.850
<i>I shall set all the missiles
aboard this ship</i>

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.980
<i>to rain down upon the islands of Japan.</i>

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:41.690
<i>Among them is one
that is equipped with a nuclear warhead.</i>

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:42.950
What?

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:47.070
<i>Even if there are any poor souls
still surviving on the islands,</i>

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:50.910
<i>this will ensure that they rest in peace.</i>

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:54.120
<i>I am also setting this ship
to self-destruct.</i>

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.460
What? Wait a second!

00:20:56.460 --> 00:21:00.000
<i>We, as the proud Japanese people,</i>

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:04.130
<i>have bravely decided to draw the curtain
on everything.</i>

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.720
<i>I think it's been long enough.</i>

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.770
<i>We've exerted more than enough effort!</i>

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:14.430
Wait just a damn minute!
What are you saying?

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:17.520
<i>I will begin the countdown now.</i>

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.860
<i>At the same time,
the ship will orient itself vertically</i>

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.690
<i>so that the missiles can be launched.</i>

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.540
Shigeru?

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:37.790
Shigeru! I've been looking for you!

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:39.960
Ango?

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:41.960
Ukai...

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.920
<i>As the Japanese people who survived
this unprecedented disaster...</i>

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:49.720
<i>No, as the last remnants of humanity,</i>

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.720
<i>let us spend this final day in peace.</i>

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:56.180
I'm glad to see you, Ango.

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:58.480
Ukai, you bastard!

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:04.150
<i>Lastly, I bring you
the poem for this morning.</i>

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.910
<i>It's by Samuel Taylor Coleridge.</i>

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:12.410
<i>An excerpt from</i>
The Rime of the Ancient Mariner.

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:14.700
Ukai!

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.040
Shigeru died because of you!
